    "text_167550914232333": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:title": "Supporting",
      "cq:masterBuildingBlock": true,
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "hannah.white@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed May 25 2022 14:27:36 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "cq/experience-fragments/editor/components/buildingblock",
      "text_1675509142323333238645613631253": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "hannah.white@stryker.com",
        "text": "<h2><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-8em\">Military appreciation at Stryker means listening to healthcare professionals who care for military members</span></span></h2>\n<p>Part of making healthcare better is listening, because you can’t solve a challenge unless you understand the problem first. This applies not only to customer feedback, but also to healthcare challenges that affect entire populations.</p>\n<p>Arthritis is a common condition among those who have served in the military, and impacts over one in three veterans – a higher rate than in the general population of US adults.<sup>1</sup></p>\n",
        "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Apr 20 2023 19:03:23 GMT+0000",
        "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
